# 3. CORE ARCHITECTURAL RULES

## 3.1 EMULATOR IS PURE EXECUTION LAYER
- No UI logic inside engine adapters
- No GRID logic inside emulator core
- No ROM acquisition inside engines

---

## 3.2 GRID IS NAVIGATION ONLY
- selects cartridges
- routes execution requests
- NEVER executes ROMs directly

---

## 3.3 ROMLOADER IS LOCAL-FIRST (CRITICAL)

PRIMARY FLOW:

User selects file (mobile or desktop)
  → romloader.js
  → ArrayBuffer normalization
  → cartridge-builder.js
  → runtime-controller.js

RULE:
- GitHub ROM fetching is OPTIONAL
- LOCAL FILES are the primary system input

---

# 4. ROMLOADER SYSTEM (LOCAL-FIRST DESIGN)

## romloader.js

RESPONSIBILITIES:
- File input handling
- Local filesystem ROM ingestion
- Buffer normalization

INPUT TYPES:
- File object (mobile/desktop)
- Drag & drop file
- Optional future URL input

OUTPUT:
- ArrayBuffer (standardized ROM payload)

RULE:
NO EMULATION LOGIC HERE

